28:55.880 --> 28:59.880
of a Elizabethan court poet
playwright named Edward Devere,

28:59.880 --> 29:01.880
who, more and more evidence
suggests,

29:01.880 --> 29:04.880
wrote under the pen name William
Shakespeare.

29:05.880 --> 29:08.880
Devere led an amazing and epic
and very Shakespearean life.

29:08.880 --> 29:11.880
He got into an interfamily war
between his family

29:11.880 --> 29:13.880
and his mistress's family,

29:13.880 --> 29:15.880
regular Elizabethan monogues and
capilets.

29:15.880 --> 29:18.880
Devere spent a year touring
France and Italy,

29:18.880 --> 29:20.880
visiting the locations where
many Shakespeare plays

29:20.880 --> 29:22.880
with later be said.

29:22.880 --> 29:24.880
Devere's sister was a
temperamental fireball

29:24.880 --> 29:26.880
who was wooed by a swashbuckler,

29:26.880 --> 29:27.880
named Paragon Birdie,

29:27.880 --> 29:29.880
and this courtship is spoofed

29:29.880 --> 29:31.880
in Shakespeare's Taming of the
